A good place to read spellbooks is behind a boulder in Sokoban.  You 
can't teleport, and the game will [try] not to create monsters in your 
line of sight.  Keep your pet with you as a guard.

 ------  -----
 |....|  |...|
 |@f..----...|
 |......0....|
 |..--->---..|
 |---------.--

The zero is the boulder.

Also, price-ID the books first, and use the formulas in spl1-343.txt to 
figure out your chance of casting them once you do learn them; there is 
no point in learning a high-level spell right away if you won't be able 
to cast it until you gain a robe and ten more levels and lots of stat 
boosts.

Generally speaking, spells of levels 1-3 can be easily cast, and have 
relatively minor penalties for failed readings.  Spells of levels 4+ 
will paralyze you dangerously long, and are likely to have 100% fail 
rates anyway at this stage of the game.

Don't forget to hide away or drop your gold before reading.


